[[:db/retract 17592186196500 :answer-field/choices 17592186196504] [:db/retract 17592186196500 :answer-field/choices 17592186196501] [:db/retract 17592186196500 :answer-field/choices 17592186196502] [:db/retract 17592186196500 :answer-field/choices 17592186196503] {:db/id 17592186198868 :question/problem "Describe the set $S=\\{-4,-3,-2,-1,0,1,…\\}$ using a conditional definition.\n\n$$\nS=\\{x\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,x>{{field-2}}\\}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The set $S$ contains all integers greater than $-4,$ including $-4.$\n\nIn other words, $S$ contains all integers greater than $-5,$ *excluding* $-5.$ \n\nTherefore, the set can be written as\n\n$$\nS=\\{x\\in Z\\,:\\,x>-5\\}.\n$$\n\n**Note**: This definition is not unique. For example:\n\n- We can write $x\\ge -4.$ This gives\n\n$$\nS=\\{x\\in Z\\,:\\,x\\ge -4\\}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186196462 :answer-field/correct 17592186196464 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186196458 :answer-field/correct 17592186196460 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186287849 :question/problem "Find the missing coefficients in the conditional definition of the set $\\{-\\frac{1}{2},3\\}$ given below.\n\n$\\{-\\frac{1}{2},3\\}=\\{q\\in Q\\,:\\,4{q}^{2}\\,-$\n{{field-1}}\n$q\\,-$\n{{field-2}}\n$=0\\}$" :question/worked-solution "The given set contains the roots $q\\in Q$ of some quadratic polynomial $p(q).$\n\nSince the quadratic polynomial has roots ${q}_{1}=-\\frac{1}{2}$ and ${q}_{2}=3,$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=4,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(q) & =a(q-{q}_{1})(q-{q}_{2}) \\\\  & =4\\cdot (q-(-\\frac{1}{2}))(q-3) \\\\  & =4(q+\\frac{1}{2})(q-3) \\\\  & =4({q}^{2}-\\frac{5q}{2}-\\frac{3}{2}) \\\\  & =4{q}^{2}-10q-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the given set as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{-\\frac{1}{2},3\\}=\\{q\\in Q\\,:\\,4{q}^{2}-10q-6=0\\}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186287853 :question/problem "Find the missing coefficients in the conditional definition of the set $\\{1\\pm \\text{i}\\}$ given below.\n\n$\\{1\\pm \\text{i}\\}=\\{z\\in C\\,:\\,2{z}^{2}\\,-$\n{{field-1}}\n$z\\,+$\n{{field-2}}\n$=0\\}$" :question/worked-solution "The given set contains the roots $z\\in C$ of some quadratic polynomial $p(z).$\n\nSince the quadratic polynomial has roots ${z}_{1}=1-\\text{i}$ and ${z}_{2}=1+\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=2,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(z) & =a(z-{z}_{1})(z-{z}_{2}) \\\\  & =2\\cdot (z-(1-\\text{i}))(z-(1+\\text{i})) \\\\  & =2\\cdot ({z}^{2}-(1-\\text{i})z-(1+\\text{i})z+(1-\\text{i})(1+\\text{i})) \\\\  & =2\\cdot ({z}^{2}-(1-\\text{i}+1+\\text{i})z+((1)^{2}-(\\text{i})^{2})) \\\\  & =2\\cdot ({z}^{2}-(2)z+(1+1)) \\\\  & =2{z}^{2}-4z+4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the given set as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{1\\pm \\text{i}\\}=\\{z\\in C\\,:\\,2{z}^{2}-4z+4=0\\}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198873 :question/problem "Describe the set $S=\\{-5,-10,-20,-40,...\\}$ using a constructive definition.\n\n$$\nS=\\{{{field-1}}\\,:\\,n\\in {{field-2}}\\}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the elements of our set\n\n$$\n-5,\\,-10,\\,-20,\\,-40,\\,…\n$$\n\nform an infinite geometric sequence with a common ratio $r=2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =2 \\\\  & =\\frac{-10}{-5} \\\\  & =\\frac{-20}{-10} \\\\  & =\\frac{-40}{-20} \\\\  & =⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $n$th term ${a}_{n}$ of our sequence for $n\\in N,$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{n-1} \\\\  & =(-5)\\cdot {2}^{n-1} \\\\  & =(-5)\\cdot {2}^{n}\\cdot {2}^{-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{2}\\cdot {2}^{n}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can define our set using a constructive definition as follows:\n\n$$\nS=\\{-\\frac{5}{2}\\cdot {2}^{n}\\,:\\,n\\in N\\}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186196500 :answer-field/correct "answer-1992cc29-bfe9-5821-ab65-85db7c9275d1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-cde8a085-4109-5cb9-b7e6-882a1aca743e" "answer-fbe45b33-5883-51ed-9f7c-2fa52c2e29d6" "answer-288cc4b2-c914-5214-82ea-49b388ebac4a" "answer-1992cc29-bfe9-5821-ab65-85db7c9275d1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cde8a085-4109-5cb9-b7e6-882a1aca743e" :answer/id #uuid "cde8a085-4109-5cb9-b7e6-882a1aca743e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5\\cdot {2}^{n}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fbe45b33-5883-51ed-9f7c-2fa52c2e29d6" :answer/id #uuid "fbe45b33-5883-51ed-9f7c-2fa52c2e29d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {5}^{n}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-288cc4b2-c914-5214-82ea-49b388ebac4a" :answer/id #uuid "288cc4b2-c914-5214-82ea-49b388ebac4a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot {2}^{n}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1992cc29-bfe9-5821-ab65-85db7c9275d1" :answer/id #uuid "1992cc29-bfe9-5821-ab65-85db7c9275d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{2}\\cdot {2}^{n}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186196496 :answer-field/correct 17592186196499 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186287864 :question/problem "Describe the set $S=\\{2,1,\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{1}{4},...\\}$ using a constructive definition.\n\n$$\nS=\\{{{field-1}}\\,:\\,n\\in {{field-2}}\\}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the elements of our set\n\n$$\n2,\\,1,\\,\\frac{1}{2},\\,\\frac{1}{4},\\,…\n$$\n\nform an infinite geometric sequence with a common ratio $r=\\frac{1}{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{1}{2}}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{1}{4}}{\\frac{1}{2}} \\\\  & =⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $n$th term ${a}_{n}$ of our sequence for $n\\in N,$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{n-1} \\\\  & =2\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{2})}^{n-1} \\\\  & =2\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{2})}^{n}\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{2})}^{-1} \\\\  & =4\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{2})}^{n}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can define our set using a constructive definition as follows:\n\n$$\nS=\\{4\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{2})}^{n}\\,:\\,n\\in N\\}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "activity-55d163d3-8f28-5869-a65b-cfaaab7569eb" :activity/id #uuid "55d163d3-8f28-5869-a65b-cfaaab7569eb" :activity/title "Describing Sets Using Set-Builder Notation" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049076 :activity/course 17592186046658 :activity/steps ["step-43789ff6-ead3-53a4-9c70-d7e0bdd62fe0" "step-b48819c1-8133-563a-afd7-f37f211bbce6" "step-e3ae9ce9-3f42-51dc-87d2-39964c93e221" "step-3a19ba88-b779-5826-958c-8abfa367305b" "step-e1124dcc-a673-55f5-863e-080064a239ce"] :activity/first-step "step-43789ff6-ead3-53a4-9c70-d7e0bdd62fe0" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-43789ff6-ead3-53a4-9c70-d7e0bdd62fe0" :step/id #uuid "43789ff6-ead3-53a4-9c70-d7e0bdd62fe0" :step/content 17592186198868 :step/next "step-b48819c1-8133-563a-afd7-f37f211bbce6" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-b48819c1-8133-563a-afd7-f37f211bbce6" :step/id #uuid "b48819c1-8133-563a-afd7-f37f211bbce6" :step/content 17592186287849 :step/next "step-e3ae9ce9-3f42-51dc-87d2-39964c93e221" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-e3ae9ce9-3f42-51dc-87d2-39964c93e221" :step/id #uuid "e3ae9ce9-3f42-51dc-87d2-39964c93e221" :step/content 17592186287853 :step/next "step-3a19ba88-b779-5826-958c-8abfa367305b" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-3a19ba88-b779-5826-958c-8abfa367305b" :step/id #uuid "3a19ba88-b779-5826-958c-8abfa367305b" :step/content 17592186198873 :step/next "step-e1124dcc-a673-55f5-863e-080064a239ce" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-e1124dcc-a673-55f5-863e-080064a239ce" :step/id #uuid "e1124dcc-a673-55f5-863e-080064a239ce" :step/content 17592186287864 :db/ensure [:step/val